0.16
----
Added "Here > Stay in place" menu item for the "." command.
"." is now countable, e.g. "20." waits 20 turns.
The 5-way navigator (Tungsten C etc.) walks north/south/west/east;
  plain Up/Down buttons walk north/south unless rebound.
Stores show their stock as an Item | Gold table, one row per item; the
  selected item's full name and weight appear below it. The store's
  Options > Compact? item is gone (it is always one row now). Fixed the
  store menu falling through into the pen-tap handler.
Walking into a closed door opens it (like NetHack's autoopen) instead of
  just saying it's in the way; locked doors get a lock-pick attempt.
The "Big font" preference now defaults to off, so a new install starts
  with the small map font.
About box, Instructions and the "can't run" screens now point to
  github.com/z88kat/palm-roguelike instead of the old email/SourceForge.
Tidied the About box: dropped the old Half-Dead Spider logo, centred the
  layout and added the release date after the version.
License screen credits the v0.16 update; History now covers Moria's 2008
  move to the GNU GPL, today's Umoria, and the 2026 revival.
License now opens a scrolling text in the normal font instead of a screen
  drawn in the tiny map font; the same text greets a new player.
`make` now puts the .prc and .pdb files to install in kMoria/build/.
New kMoria-manual.pdb: a Palm DOC e-book of MANUAL.md plus the rules
  chapters of the Moria manual, built by make.
New, brighter colour scheme in kMoriaColorDB.pdb that reads on both the
  white and the Invert (black) background. Walls and @ stay plain.

0.15 - for the next release
---------------------------
Fixed the 'recall' bug, you now remember multiple attack types properly.
Hardware button bindings in 'look' form: up/down for next,
  datebook/address to recall (when applicable), todo/memopad to exit
Hardware button bindings in 'recall' form: down for next (also up/down
  to scroll), datebook/address/todo/memopad to exit
Fixed map bug that could crash non-color devices in an inverted map screen.
  ....However this causes a new problem: on some Sony device the code in
  display.c to print inverted characters in the dungeon doesn't invert now
  (the stats area still inverts ok)
Fixed crash bug in exchange_weap: buffer for "Primary weapon: <name>" was
   too short for weapons with long names, e.g. a studly Zweihander.
[ time passes ]
Increased max count to 999 (default for auto-repeat commands is still 99);
  reduced the delay for all.  I made it print the "Repeat %d" less often.
Made hjklyubnHJLKYUBN "countable", so you should be able to say "20h" now;
  "20h" is just like "H", except that it will go for at most 20 paces.
You can write the initial letter of inventory buttons (e=eat, ..., D=Done).
  Case-sensitive!  Lower-case will only work after an item is selected.
New save databases are set to "backup".  Existing ones are not touched yet.
"Shift" will make hjkl-bound buttons into HJKL-bound (i.e. you run).
  Note: You can't attack things that you are next to, when shift is on.
kMoria will now checkpoint the save file every 200 turns if you are
  not resting; 2000 turns if you are resting a whole lot.
Monsters/objects will compact now when there are too many; you should
  see "Compacting monsters.." when farming rather than just crash.

0.14 - current release
----------------------
* Handera users can now experience an entirely new set of bugs!
  (The Handera support has been tested only on the POSE emulator, not on
  the real thing.  Be wary and please report any problems.)
    + kMoria uses Handera's small font for the small font.
    + The virtual Graffiti area can be frobbed to expand the screen.
    + Write 'R' to rotate the display...
      - The Rotation command is available in the main screen only.
      - The character generation screen reverts to 0-degree rotation.
* Preferences screen is rearranged into 2 parts, "display" and "moving",
  with three new preferences (initially set to "maintain status quo").
    + new preference to turn off animations for missiles/spells
      (Doesn't affect animation of breath attacks; should it?)
    + new preference to prompt for user when kMoria starts up
      (for multi-user Palms; like tapping Menu->Set->User immediately)
    + new preference to select most recent user when kMoria starts up,
      or just highlight the most recent one if prompt-for-user is on
* Keyboard users: in the Map screen, type '@' to tap on the @ button.
* Added/removed a couple of main-menu shortcuts.  Added 'g' to menu.
* Some more of the bugs introduced with the 'g' command are cleaned up:
    + hardware buttons should work for directional commands
      (e.g. opening/closing doors)
    + detect-{monsters,invisible,evil} message should clear properly.
    + what's-that command (/) should work.
    + move-by-tapping and nondirectional spells can be "again"ed.

Known bugs:
- Modal forms (e.g. prompt to pick up an item) that use FrmAlert() cannot
  override the application buttons.  (So if you are heading east with
  enthusiasm you'll wind up in the ToDo list.)  Not very fixable.
- Handera support could use more work, e.g. the Map screen is not fabulous.


PREVIOUS CHANGES
----------------

0.13
        Bug fix: Keyboard arrow keys will work for directional commands.
        Repeated commands can be interrupted by keyboard now.
        In the Learn Spell form, keyboard users can select spells by letter.
        Targeting-circles preference is somewhat less broken now.
              (But does anyone actually want it?)
0.12
        New application icon: doors of Moria
        Winning should work now (don't exit before seeing the scoreboard).
        New command 'g' for "again"; can be bound to a button.
              (Many exciting new bugs were introduced simultaneously!)
        Spell book does not wait for you to press Return (for keyboard).
        In color, the /M map uses your defined foreground/background colors.
        Longer message log.
        Level-changing messages print _during_ the dungeon level creation.
        Shorter delay for repeated commands.
        In the User selection screen, you can set the Hotsync bit for saves.
	(For keyboards) the Haggle form grabs focus when you type numbers.
        You can beam cash.  Woo hoo.
0.11
        "Beam" menu choice: kMoria itself; your top score; an inventory item
        "User" menu choice: you can have several concurrent save databases
        'Rest' form buttons bound to the 4 app buttons
        Item weight is displayed in stores (thanks to dan_van)
        'Show time' menu item will show current date/time and battery voltage
        Arrow keys act like 'hjkl' for stowaway keyboard users
        The button bound to 'map' will also exit from 'map'.
        Fixed the Chunk-Overlocked bug from 0.10.
0.10
        Fixed "fails to detect no saved character" bug from 0.09
        The Your Stats screen highlights drained stats.
        Source code for [unsupported] pdb<->umoria save file converter
        [Forgot to update version in the 0.10 About screen: still says 0.09]
0.09
        Color.  Install and use kMoriaUtil to set the colors.
        Invert (more or less working)
        "Open door", "font", etc. can now be bound to hardware buttons too.
        When casting a spell you can hit the 4 app buttons for spellbook.
        You can assign hardware buttons to any of the spells.
        You can set some of the repeatable commands to autorepeat.
        Fixed the stone-to-mud monster-killing crash.
        Directional prayers are fixed (used to take 2 turns, now take 1).
        Command-bar bug (for OS 3.5) fixed; icons added.
        Fixed the wielding-thing-when-already-wielding-cursed-weapon msg.
        The Repeat count is cleared when it is interrupted.
        Stats update should be a little smarter now.
        Font ID++.  If you have a Kyocera, let me know if this helped.
        Score is reset between characters now.
        Shopkeeper bug fixed (if you got booted, the store owner got 
          clobbered by a General Store owner.)
        License stuff has been clarified.
0.08
        Recovery of crashed save files.  Minor bug fixes.
0.07
        Tap the [@] button in the Map to make your position flash briefly.
        Write a letter after '/' command, to recall ALL that-letter monsters.
        When recalling monsters, there's a menu item to clear your "memory".
        Should be safe to export dead character to memo now.
        Fixed crosshairs for directional spells (were appearing "too late").
        Made hit points 'usually' not get overwritten by graffiti indicator.
        Made directional acts print the verb, e.g. "Throwing"
        Plugged memory leaks in store, inventory, equipment, and invselect.
        Twiddled the store form in a few ways:
        1. When the store is "full", the last screen says so.
        2. Made the "You have" "You've sold" (in haggling form) word-wrapped.
        3. Tweaked the truncation of item names in store list.
        Fixed look-at so the dungeon is always drawn up at the top.
0.06
        Counted commands (like rest) can be interrupted now, tap the screen.
        Directional commands with pie slices should now redraw properly always.
        Fixed bug that sometimes didn't draw a new dungeon level.
        When you climb stairs, the event queue is flushed on general principle.
        Going back from screen 0 in a shop should not produce empty screen now.
        Hardware buttons that are bound stay disabled in all Forms.
        Running stops before hitting a stationary creature (but it can hit you)
        Made "HJKLYUBJN" run instead of walk; other keyboard-friendly things.
        Fixed bug so that selling an unknown thing to store makes it known.
        [Checked what the amulet of resist acid is supposed to do.  not a bug.]
0.05
        Acid/corrosion bug and relative-move bug fixed.  I think.
        Inventory has optional weight display (menu item).
        Hit points always visible in the last message of the turn.
        Preference to move status bar to top of screen.
        Command-count should understand 'delete' character now.
        Animation for throw, spells, + breath attacks.
        Some sound added.
        Potions, food, monster special attacks + monster spells got tested.
        Detects wrong-version-for-OS and missing-database at startup.
0.04
        High score list.
        Menus re-organized.
        User can reassign hardware buttons.
        Overview map and 'look' are improved.
        Throw, inscribe, resting should work now.
        Write a letter to select item in the inventory view.
        Item names are not truncated in equipment, inventory, + stores.
        There is another menu item in the stores to turn off haggling.
        Scrolls, spells, prayers, wands, staffs all enabled, tested.
        Some bugs fixed.
0.03
        Fixed many small bugs.
        Status words (e.g. "Hungry") are displayed now (but still buggy).
        Characters with negative hit points die (but no high score list yet).
        Tombstone page allows Character Record export to memo.
        Screen redraw made less sluggish.
0.02
        Saving the game (when you leave the application) works.
        You can quit the game and start a new character.
        Some bugs (most frequent, most evil) have been removed.
0.01
        first alpha release.
